WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.566 --> 00:00:03.566
(logo reverberates)

2
00:00:05.566 --> 00:00:07.233
- So we're really rolling now.

3
00:00:07.233 --> 00:00:11.766
We've got our enemy that
rolls towards our player,

4
00:00:11.766 --> 00:00:15.666
and it's not moving at
an incredibly fast speed.

5
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:19.733
So, one real quick thing
that we're gonna do,

6
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:23.066
is we're just going to
clean up some of our code.

7
00:00:23.066 --> 00:00:25.366
So, in our update function

8
00:00:25.366 --> 00:00:29.466
we have this really
long line of code here,

9
00:00:29.466 --> 00:00:32.833
so we're actually just going
to clean this up a little bit

10
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:34.566
by using one variable.

11
00:00:34.566 --> 00:00:37.466
Now, because in our update
function is the only place

12
00:00:37.466 --> 00:00:39.833
that we're really going to be calculating

13
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:41.500
the position of the player

14
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.133
against the current position of the enemy,

15
00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.933
this is where we're going
to create our variable

16
00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:48.233
so that we don't need it anywhere else.

17
00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:50.033
So we're going to create a Vector3,

18
00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:54.833
because we're taking in
two different positions,

19
00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:58.033
our player and our current transform.

20
00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:01.466
We'll call this Vector3 the lookDirection.

21
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.933
So this'll actually be the direction

22
00:01:05.933 --> 00:01:08.900
that the enemy will be moving towards.

23
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:13.200
We're going to set this,

24
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.700
and we're actually just
gonna take this line of code.

25
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.466
We can cut it and paste it,

26
00:01:20.966 --> 00:01:23.800
and then we'll close off with a semicolon.

27
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:28.266
Now, the reason why we
keep our equation here

28
00:01:28.266 --> 00:01:31.100
still in parenthesis,
is just so that we can

29
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.100
use the .normalized,

30
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.200
so that way we can apply
our normalized vector

31
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.700
on to the final vector that
comes out of this position here.

32
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.300
So now that we have that in our AddForce,

33
00:01:47.166 --> 00:01:49.633
we can just put lookDirection.

34
00:01:51.266 --> 00:01:54.466
And when we save, if we test our game,

35
00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:58.966
you can see that the enemy is still moving

36
00:01:58.966 --> 00:02:00.900
at the same speed towards the player.

37
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.166
So, now it's your turn.

38
00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:08.766
In your Update method,
you're going to create

39
00:02:08.766 --> 00:02:12.766
a new Vector3 variable for the direction

40
00:02:12.766 --> 00:02:15.233
that our enemy's going to move towards.

41
00:02:15.233 --> 00:02:17.366
You're going to take the equation

42
00:02:17.366 --> 00:02:21.166
that we had in our AddForce
for the player's position

43
00:02:21.166 --> 00:02:24.166
minus the enemy's current position.

44
00:02:24.166 --> 00:02:27.566
And then you're gonna
normalize that entire vector,

45
00:02:27.566 --> 00:02:30.066
so that way it doesn't
increase in magnitude

46
00:02:30.066 --> 00:02:32.733
the farther the two objects are away.

47
00:02:32.733 --> 00:02:35.866
And then, your lookDirection
you'll just add

48
00:02:35.866 --> 00:02:37.700
into your AddForce.

49
00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.400
Now it's your turn.

50
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.400
(logo reverberates)
